<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38295" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prīdĭānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		pridie, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the day
				before</i>, <i>that happened</i>, <i>was used</i>, <i>eaten</i>, etc., <i>the day before</i>, <i>yesterday's</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pridiana ac semesa opsonia apposuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 34</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Vit. 13</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Calig. 58</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">balinea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 19, 77, § 248</span></i>
			: reliquiae, Cat. ap. <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 277,
				13</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pluvia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 7, p. 196, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pruina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 11</span></i>
			, p. 260, 19. 
			</div>
